    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d448-a1">

                <pb facs="0690" n="670" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg670"/>

                <head>Mr. Welles to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Navy Department,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-07-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 30, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 21st instant, enclosing a copy of a note addressed to you
                    on the 11th instant, by Lord Lyons, in reference to two apprentice boys
                    belonging to the British ship Cuzco, who, it is said, deserted from that vessel
                    at Valparaiso, and were received on board the United States ship St. Mary’s.
                    Acting Rear-Admiral Charles H. Bell has been directed to investigate the
                    matter.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, &amp;c, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GIDEON WELLES, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the
                        Navy,</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State,&amp;c.,&amp;c.,&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
